ddressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI ELECTRIC CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NARIKAWA MASAFUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUMOTO, WATARU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI DENKI KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NARIKAWA, MASAFUMI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUMOTO WATARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NARIKAWA MASAFUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUMOTO, WATARU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NARIKAWA, MASAFUMI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>The TTR of an ATU-C is delayed by S1, and the TTR transmitted to another ATU-R being the communication party is adjusted by S2 by delaying or advancing. Thereby, all the interferences occurring between a TCM-ISDN and an ADSL both of which communicate by using the line having the same characteristics and the same reference signal, and all the interferences occurring between the ADSLs are eliminated.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne un dispositif de communication dans lequel la référence temps (TTR) d'un ATU-C est retardée de S1, et la référence temps émise à un autre ATU-R partageant la communication est ajustée de S2 par retard ou avance. Ce mode de fonctionnement permet de supprimer toutes les interférences qui se produisent entre un multiplexage par compression dans le temps RNIS (TCM-ISDN) et une ligne d'abonné numérique asymétrique (ADSL), tous les deux communicant sur une ligne possédant les mêmes caractéristiques et le même signal de référence, ainsi que toutes les interférences se produisant entre des ADSL.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>